# Disposition from affinity (DESIGN.md §8.1): how an observer regards a character, from how
# close their alignments are. Until M4 the score is the affinity alone: the affinity curve
# applied to the distance.
load content/sample
disposition city_watch player --explain
assert disposition temple sister_mira == 45.34 (friendly)
assert disposition temple brother_ash == -32.15 (unfriendly)
assert disposition city_watch vex == -23.36 (neutral)
# A character judges by their own lights: Vex sees the neutral player as barely neutral.
assert disposition vex player == 1.23 (neutral)
# Thieving brings the player closer to the Lantern Guild, and it warms to them.
assert disposition lantern_guild player == -0.08 (neutral)
act player steal --scale 4
assert disposition lantern_guild player == 16.66 (neutral)
assert disposition player temple == error: a disposition's subject must be a character

# Bands are content: this world adds hostile below unfriendly.
load crates/cli/tests/fixtures/worlds/hostile
disposition temple brother_ash --explain
